;; The language version pyi's runtime follows (queue 237, doc/python/PY315-SURVEY.md §2 P4a): Python 3.14 by default, 3.15
;; under REPR_PYTHON_VERSION=3.15, the reader's switch (queue 236: arbace.repr.python.lex/*minor*), so a program is read
;; and run by one version. Under 3.14 nothing changes; under 3.15 the names 3.15 adds are present (sentinel, frozendict,
;; math.integer, slice[...], bytearray.take_bytes, ImportError's keyword repr, __slots__ on a tuple subclass, UTF-8 by
;; default). sys.version_info stays 3.14.10's until the standard library moves with it (P7: the pin, the records).



